"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:26:24-07:00","id":464120,"title":"","content":"I dunno, the section on Bloodlines pretty explicitly states that no-one outside of a Bloodline can learn that Bloodline's unique Discipline (if it has one), so... (I'm going off B&amp;S, here.)<br /> <br /> Still, Sublunario can be ignored in favour of taking the _____ Moon's Birth merits. I mean, if being a Ghoul doesn't strip you of those (that's <i>explicitly</i> your ST's call, so YTMV).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:15:52-07:00","id":464168,"title":"","content":"Ghouls have always been able to learn their master's disciplines, even the unique bloodline disciplines, the only exception being blood magic for social reasons (the covenants don't like ghouls learning their magics), and the powers of the ordo dracul metaphysically, because ghouls aren't vampires.<br /> <br /> That probably won't change in vampire second edition, and even if it did, unique disciplines are largely being replaced with bloodline advantages and devotions, so if they're devotions they'd be available to ghouls.<br /> <br /> So even if they change the rules in the future, there's a good shot that they'd be turned into devotions that a ghoul could still learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:50:49-07:00","id":464196,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected (stupid checking the Bloodline rules and not the Ghoul rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}